  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Find ${y}^{\u2032}$ for $y=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(2{x}^{3}+x).$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(2{x}^{3}+x)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{(2{x}^{3}+x)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(2{x}^{3}+x)^{2}}\\cdot (6{x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}+1}{1+(2{x}^{3}+x)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
